(689883, 72334, 13035, '<td valign="top">A very relaxing and attractive shot.  Very similar to last weeks blue ribbon.  I have high hopes for you.  As far as advanced digital editing goes, the blown out whites and the absolute dead gray/blue tones in the sky need repaired.  I would select out the entire sky, and paint in a blue one with some happy white clouds.  While the broken bench adds character to the scene, it doesn''t help me to feel like I want to sit there to enjoy this wonderful overlook.  And since I''m assuming that you have included the bench to create exactly that emotion, you should fix the bench.  Take out the broken board, and patch in a replacement.  Very nice image. 9</td>', 'A very relaxing and attractive shot.  Very similar to last weeks blue ribbon.  I have high hopes for you.  As far as advanced digital editing goes, the blown out whites and the absolute dead gray/blue tones in the sky need repaired.  I would select out the entire sky, and paint in a blue one with some happy white clouds.  While the broken bench adds character to the scene, it doesn''t help me to feel like I want to sit there to enjoy this wonderful overlook.  And since I''m assuming that you have included the bench to create exactly that emotion, you should fix the bench.  Take out the broken board, and patch in a replacement.  Very nice image. 9', '2004-04-28 21:48:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(689891, 72230, 13035, '<td valign="top">An absolutely wonderful shot.  I have it in my top 5.  From an advanced editing standpoint, I think that you missed a little on the crop.  I would find this more attractive had you balanced the space between the borders and your right and left fence posts.  The very tall fence post directly in the center conflicts with the wonderful triangulation that you receive from the fencepost that tilts to the right.  I would ask that you cut in off directly above the barbed-wire, and patch in a little hillside, and the sky.  I cheering for a ribbon from you.  9</td>', 'An absolutely wonderful shot.  I have it in my top 5.  From an advanced editing standpoint, I think that you missed a little on the crop.  I would find this more attractive had you balanced the space between the borders and your right and left fence posts.  The very tall fence post directly in the center conflicts with the wonderful triangulation that you receive from the fencepost that tilts to the right.  I would ask that you cut in off directly above the barbed-wire, and patch in a little hillside, and the sky.  I cheering for a ribbon from you.  9', '2004-04-28 21:56:04.000000', NULL, 1),
